WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.630 --> 00:00:02.760
Hi, my name is Zareen Choudhury.

00:00:02.760 --> 00:00:05.580
And I'm a master's student
in electrical engineering

00:00:05.580 --> 00:00:06.990
and computer science.

00:00:06.990 --> 00:00:08.970
And for my master's
research, I've

00:00:08.970 --> 00:00:12.650
been working in the networks
at MIT group in C-cell.

00:00:12.650 --> 00:00:15.270
The main technology
that our group works on

00:00:15.270 --> 00:00:19.050
is a device called WiTrack
which is a wall mounted

00:00:19.050 --> 00:00:22.170
IoT device that uses
radio signals to monitor

00:00:22.170 --> 00:00:24.880
various things of people
in the environment,

00:00:24.880 --> 00:00:28.630
such as their breathing,
sleeping, and walking patterns.

00:00:28.630 --> 00:00:30.630
Now in order to
actually use this device

00:00:30.630 --> 00:00:32.670
and deploy it in
people's homes there

00:00:32.670 --> 00:00:35.790
are two main components that
first need to be configured,

00:00:35.790 --> 00:00:38.790
which are connecting the
device to a wireless network

00:00:38.790 --> 00:00:41.730
for internet connectivity
and specifying

00:00:41.730 --> 00:00:43.860
the boundaries in
which the device is

00:00:43.860 --> 00:00:45.620
allowed to collect data.

00:00:45.620 --> 00:00:47.910
Now unfortunately, the
pre-existing methods

00:00:47.910 --> 00:00:50.310
for configuring both
of these components

00:00:50.310 --> 00:00:53.340
was very difficult to
use, required experts,

00:00:53.340 --> 00:00:55.200
and was not always reliable.

00:00:55.200 --> 00:00:56.890
So for my project.

00:00:56.890 --> 00:01:00.480
I built the first configuration
system for WiTrack

00:01:00.480 --> 00:01:04.230
for both wireless connectivity
and physical boundaries.

00:01:04.230 --> 00:01:08.100
And I focused on making
this system easy to use,

00:01:08.100 --> 00:01:13.020
not requiring experts, as well
as being reliable and robust.

00:01:13.020 --> 00:01:15.180
And as of now,
we've successfully

00:01:15.180 --> 00:01:17.820
deployed the wireless
configuration system

00:01:17.820 --> 00:01:20.730
in over a dozen homes with
successful and positive

00:01:20.730 --> 00:01:21.870
feedback.

00:01:21.870 --> 00:01:23.640
And we are currently
in the process

00:01:23.640 --> 00:01:26.130
of running user studies
for the configuration

00:01:26.130 --> 00:01:28.444
for physical boundaries.

